WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.520
We're The Office ladies.

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.940
Before we get going today, I want to say happy birthday to my BFF.

9
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.560
Thank you, Angela.

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:42.380
Yes, as I was arriving today, I saw Angela not open the door for me and instead run past the door because she was up to something.

11
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.980
I didn't think you saw me.

12
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.320
Although Sam and Cassie, I did say there's a chance she might have seen me.

13
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.100
I did say that.

14
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:48.480
Yes, you did.

15
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.940
I did that right after I swatted plastic cutlery out of Sam's hand.

16
00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.100
It was the most aggressive thing I've ever seen you do.

17
00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.280
No time, no time.

18
00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.300
No time, she's here.

19
00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.780
Get the cutlery out of the way.

20
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.020
But we love you and we wanted to say happy birthday.

21
00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:04.520
Oh, I loved it.

22
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.600
I got a giant bouquet of flowers.

23
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.600
I mean, humongous, so pretty.

24
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.540
And Josh made me some gluten-free treats.

25
00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.980
He did because you get desserts on your birthday at Office ladies.

26
00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:16.840
I like it.

27
00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.680
And then Angela, you gave me just a beautiful gift.

28
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:24.540
It's an inside joke, I guess we should say.

29
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:29.900
But also, guys, I made the card with my second grade level skill set.

30
00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.860
And it was an elaborate homemade card and I loved it.

31
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:33.680
Thank you.

32
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.840
Well, what are we talking about today?

33
00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:42.220
We are talking about Shareholder Meeting, which is Season 6, Episode 11, written by Justin

34
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.920
Spitzer and directed by Charles McDougal.

35
00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:45.860
Action!

36
00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:46.700
Action!

37
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:48.120
Charles McDougal.

38
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:48.520
Mm-hmm.

39
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:49.940
Here's your summary.

40
00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:56.100
Michael heads to a shareholder meeting in New York City, and he brings Andy, Dwight,

41
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:57.340
and Oscar with him.

42
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:03.920
Michael is shocked when he and other higher members of the company are booed while on

43
00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:10.680
stage, and he tries to improve the situation by suddenly and publicly making promises that

44
00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.020
management cannot fill.

45
00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:18.440
Meanwhile, back at the office, Jim realizes that nobody takes him seriously as a real boss.

46
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.000
That's our summary.

47
00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.560
Michael on a stage in front of people, what were you thinking, corporate?

48
00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.900
What were you thinking?

49
00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.900
They must have been very desperate.

50
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:29.640
Clearly.

51
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:41.740
Fast fact number one, this episode ran on November 19th, 2009 during NBC's Green Week, also known

52
00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.500
as Green is Universal.

53
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.720
Yes.

54
00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.560
For, you know, NBC Universal.

55
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.460
I remember we went to, like, a party for NBC around this time, and the red carpet was

56
00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:52.020
green.

57
00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:52.900
Yes!

58
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:54.040
The green carpet.

59
00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.780
They turned their logo green for this week as well.

60
00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:04.540
For Green Week, the network asked shows to incorporate this theme into their episodes

61
00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.040
somehow.

62
00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:12.040
They also ran news stories on environmental issues like hybrid vehicles and hydrofracking.

63
00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.160
Al Gore made an appearance on 30 Rock.

64
00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.720
On Community, the college that they attend.

65
00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.460
Greendale.

66
00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.300
It's Greendale Community College.

67
00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:24.320
Well, they changed their name to Environdale.

68
00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:26.620
They were already green!

69
00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.080
I know, but they changed it to Environdale.

70
00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.900
And then they plan a green concert.

71
00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.860
This was my favorite tie-in.

72
00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.240
On Law & Order SVU, they had, quote,

73
00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:44.340
an accused killer has to resort to alternate means to make money after too many people have

74
00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.920
started recycling their own bottles and cans.

75
00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.320
Wow.

76
00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:57.280
Which I thought was, um, it's kind of like too much recycling led to a killing spree.

77
00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:57.760
Yeah.

78
00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.580
Feels like a message maybe not what Green Week was hoping for.

79
00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.700
Feels a little forced, guys.

80
00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:05.940
No judgment.

81
00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.420
Feels a little forced.

82
00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.640
Our contribution to Green Week was Recyclops.

83
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:12.880
We have a whole cold open.

84
00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.040
Oh, Rain is Recyclops.

85
00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.220
He really got into it.

86
00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.360
Well, we got a lot of info on that.

87
00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.100
We're going to break it down for you when we get there.

88
00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:21.520
Okay.

89
00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.700
Fast fact number two is a location breakdown for the shareholder meeting.

90
00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.620
They were not in New York City.

91
00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:28.600
What?

92
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:29.880
Yeah.

93
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.620
We didn't fly there and hire all those people in Manhattan?

94
00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.960
We did not, lady.

95
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:35.780
Where was it?

96
00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:39.480
This hotel, all the interiors and the exteriors,

97
00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:44.320
were shot at the Downtown Marriott Hotel on South Figueroa in Los Angeles.

98
00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.540
Now Marriott sold this property some years back,

99
00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.560
and it is now called the L.A.

100
00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:50.300
Grand Hotel.

101
00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.960
We shot at the hotel for three days.

102
00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:56.300
On Monday and Tuesday, we were in the main ballroom,

103
00:04:56.460 --> 00:05:00.480
and we used 405 background performers each day.

104
00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:05.220
And then on Thursday, we were in the lobby and the hospitality suite

105
00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.120
and the kind of drive-up area.

106
00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:08.580
The valet?

107
00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:09.740
The valet, yeah.

108
00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.640
The drive-up area.

109
00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.660
Take me to the drive-up area.

110
00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.000
Hi, could I claim my car from the drive-up area, please?

111
00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:18.580
Thank you.

112
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.280
I have my thingy for my drive-up area.

113
00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.880
Well, Randy told us that the hotel provided us with breakfast

114
00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:29.480
and craft services for all of our background performers,

115
00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:33.520
but Sergio and Alan of Big Time Catering made lunch for everybody.

116
00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:39.220
We had to have three serving lines like we did for Company Picnic.

117
00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.440
That's a lot of people.

118
00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:41.320
They went all out.

119
00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:41.700
Yeah.

120
00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.160
All right, let's move on to Fast Fact No.

121
00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:45.480
3.

122
00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.360
I'm very excited about Fast Fact No.

123
00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:47.800
3.

124
00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.100
Here's the thing about Fast Fact No.

125
00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:51.440
3.

126
00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.440
Tell them.

127
00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:59.340
At 15 minutes and 35 seconds, there is a scene with Jim and Ryan back in the annex.

128
00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:05.500
Jim is asking Ryan if he's finished this spreadsheet that he's asked him to do,

129
00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.160
but Ryan is playing Tetris.

130
00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:14.300
This is all part of that Jim-Ryan storyline where Ryan is goofing off

131
00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.800
and no one takes Jim's authority seriously.

132
00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.960
Seriously, this episode could be called Shareholder Meeting slash Ryan Sass.

133
00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:22.340
It really could.

134
00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.560
It rolls off the tongue.

135
00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:27.860
Well, in this scene of Ryan playing Tetris,

136
00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:32.980
I noticed there were a ton of gift bags on Kelly's desk.

137
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.480
And I was like, what are all these gift bags about?

138
00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.920
I just, I had to know what's up with the gift bags.

139
00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.060
Yeah, I noticed it too.

140
00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:42.220
I counted four gift bags.

141
00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:44.100
What the heck are these gift bags about?

142
00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:47.260
I was thinking, is there something in the shooting draft?

143
00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.400
Maybe something that was deleted that could explain this.

144
00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:55.200
Well, when I went to check the shooting draft, the entire Jim-Ryan storyline,

145
00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:58.520
otherwise known as Ryan Sass, was missing.

146
00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.240
I mean, it's just not there at all.

147
00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.360
Completely not there.

148
00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:05.260
So I went to the shooting draft because I didn't know Jenna was going to the shooting draft.

149
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:06.420
And then I'm like, Jenna, what the heck?

150
00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:07.820
The Ryan Sass is gone.

151
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.480
And we started trading all these messages about it.

152
00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.400
You guys, we had a text flurry.

153
00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:14.860
We really did.

154
00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.560
And we decided to get to the bottom of it.

155
00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:23.700
Folks, fast fact number three is going to be a real mom detectives moment.

156
00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.660
Sam even made us an intro for it.

157
00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:34.780
It was a cold and rainy night when someone dropped that package through my mailbox.

158
00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.660
So many clues.

159
00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:37.720
So much chaos.

160
00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.180
It had been a long time since I saw this big of a mess.

161
00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:45.520
But because it wasn't a far drive.

162
00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.400
And because it wasn't a school night.

163
00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:53.100
And because there was only a little bit of evidence so it could fit in a small amount of pockets.

164
00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.440
And because I had snacks in case they got hungry.

165
00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.340
And because it wasn't chilly out.

166
00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.700
God help me, I knew who I needed to call.

167
00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:08.320
The mom detectives.

168
00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:12.090
I love it so much.

169
00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:15.860
A piece of that makes me laugh, Sam.

170
00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:17.720
I love that it starts in a thunderstorm.

171
00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:23.380
I love the small amount of evidence that can fit into tiny pockets.

172
00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.120
And because we have snacks.

173
00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.480
There were restrooms nearby.

174
00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:27.920
Oh, yes.

175
00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:30.660
Well, here it is, folks.

176
00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.700
I reached out to James Carey and writer Justin Spitzer.

177
00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:41.780
And I dug into my digital clutter and I found an email from Randy Cordray that said,

178
00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:47.740
Team office, it is looking like we need to shoot some additional material for shareholder meeting.

179
00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.060
Additional material.

180
00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:50.020
What does that mean?

181
00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.100
I said, Jenna, I found an email.

182
00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.780
I quickly texted her.

183
00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.400
Randy goes on to say,

184
00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:59.000
We are planning these scenes for Monday, October 19th.

185
00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:02.860
Webisodes will be moving to Tuesday, October 20th.

186
00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.500
Thank you, Randy Cordray.

187
00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:05.640
Hmm.

188
00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:06.600
Hmm.

189
00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:11.360
Well, Jenna, this was a big deal because we were supposed to go on hiatus.

190
00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:12.700
Yes.

191
00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:13.280
Right?

192
00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.160
We had this big, long hiatus starting October 19th.

193
00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.800
All the way until after the new year.

194
00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.660
A few of us were going to work on the webisodes,

195
00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.600
but the majority of the company was officially on hiatus.

196
00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:25.680
So Randy was basically saying like,

197
00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:27.020
Don't go out of town.

198
00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.080
We might need you.

199
00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:28.960
Yes.

200
00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:33.820
I found out that Steve was scheduled to shoot the movie Dinner for Schmucks.

201
00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.500
So we were shutting down production early that year.

202
00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:42.080
I spoke to James Carey, who uncovered the call sheet schedule for shareholder meeting.

203
00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.920
And it's true.

204
00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.920
We shot most of this episode the week of September 28th,

205
00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:54.200
but we did not shoot the Jim Ryan scenes until Friday, October 16th.

206
00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:55.880
I had to know why.

207
00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:57.160
The plot thickens.

208
00:09:57.980 --> 00:10:01.840
Writer Justin Spitzer told me that the Jim Ryan storyline

209
00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:06.040
was a part of his original outline for this episode,

210
00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:11.460
but it was eventually cut from the shooting draft in favor of staying at the hotel

211
00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.280
for more scenes of the shareholder meeting.

212
00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:19.080
So that plot, that Jim Ryan plot, was then shortened

213
00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:23.740
and repurposed as a cold open for Scott's Tots.

214
00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:24.480
What?

215
00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.460
We actually shot it during Scott's Tots.

216
00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:35.340
But then it was cut from Scott's Tots, and it was rewritten again,

217
00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.940
and we added that shoot day, and it went back into shareholder meeting.

218
00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:44.040
So Justin said that when they were editing shareholder meeting,

219
00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:48.880
they just missed not checking in on the group back at Dunder Mifflin.

220
00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:55.040
He also said that in all of these iterations of the Jim Ryan storyline,

221
00:10:55.040 --> 00:11:00.100
the one thing that always happened was that Ryan ended up in a closet.

222
00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:05.380
And the reason for this was that they wanted to get BJ out of the background

223
00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:08.020
of scenes that were happening in the bullpen.

224
00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:09.320
Sneaky.

225
00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:10.160
Yes.

226
00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:17.280
So that scene that we saw, Angela, that's in the annex with Ryan playing Tetris?

227
00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:17.740
Yeah.

228
00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:21.780
That was actually shot during Scott's Tots.

229
00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:25.680
That is the one scene from that cold open that remained.

230
00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:32.600
And then we added all of this other stuff about people not taking Jim seriously,

231
00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.920
and we fleshed it out.

232
00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:38.100
Well, this was clearly a puzzle, but we haven't figured it out yet.

233
00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.080
We are still wondering about these four gift bags on Kelly's desk.

234
00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:45.460
I was curious which webisode we were shooting that week,

235
00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.740
so I reached out to Randy, and he said it was The Mentor.

236
00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:53.740
In this webisode series, Erin decides she wants to learn to be an accountant.

237
00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:57.020
I rewatched it, and here's how it's set up.

238
00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:00.240
Sometimes I do get bored at reception,

239
00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.140
and I wonder what it's like to be an accountant.

240
00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:06.000
So I guess what I'm saying is I really want your life,

241
00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.020
and I don't know how to get it.

242
00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:08.140
Are you good with numbers?

243
00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.160
The count used to be my favorite part of Sesame Street.

244
00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:16.060
One apple, two apples, three apples.

245
00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.500
Ah, ah, ah, ah, ah.

246
00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:20.500
Yeah.

247
00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:21.940
Maybe it's not for you.

248
00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:28.560
I could be your mentor.

249
00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:29.640
Okay.

250
00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:30.660
Yeah, I can do it.

251
00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:32.860
I have to do everything else around here, so.

252
00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:33.880
Really?

253
00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:34.620
Yes.

254
00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:35.240
Great!

255
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.060
Oh!

256
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.020
Uh-huh.

257
00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:45.040
This whole webisode series is Angela Martin teaching Erin how to be an accountant and grooming her.

258
